From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Berg <fedora@slipsprogrammor.no>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 22:11:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Print the playback rate as "1.25x", not "1.25.x"

The position label appends the rate whenever it is not 1.0, but the format
string put a literal dot before the x, so a rate of 1.25 displayed as
"1.25.x" and 0.75 as "0.75.x". Format to two decimals and drop the stray
dot.
---
 src/main.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/main.rs b/src/main.rs
index c990050..64298e2 100644
--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -603,7 +603,7 @@ impl VideoPlayer {
                 // FIXME: Ideally it'd be nice to show this on an OSD overlay?
                 let playback_rate = video_player.player.playback_rate();
                 if playback_rate != 1.0 {
-                    format!("{status} @ {playback_rate}.x")
+                    format!("{status} @ {playback_rate:.2}x")
                 } else {
                     status
                 }
